KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20 m.cpp
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ f from the imported module: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Modules ([module]) are not supported: `import m;' is not resolved, and main
fails to type-check (CONVERSION ERROR).  A module interface unit on its own
is accepted (its `export module' declaration is ignored).  Supporting
modules needs the translation units in dependency order, with the exported
declarations of each imported module (or header unit) visible in its
importers ([module.import]/2-3, [module.reach]), rather than CBMC's
preprocessed-source model.  Checked with GCC 16 (g++ -std=c++20 -fmodules
m.cpp main.cpp): only the WRONG assertion fails.
